  "counterfactual": "At a TP exchange let P be the vector of original pack readiness and k be each rank’s removable QLI duration. Under unchanged local downstream work and immediate propagation, max(P)-max(P-k) lies between min(k) and max(k) for any rank clock offsets. Sum the four bounds only in the serial, fully propagated step scenario, charge one common full synthetic replacement per step, and accumulate over the same request’s natural full steps. No lower bound above zero on actual service gain.",
  "decision": "All natural full steps have the four stock tasks. Resolving the exact final publisher can move this local estimate only within the stored spread. The decision now depends on whether the candidate executes and how much of the saving survives the TP and later dependency joins during actual timed steps.",
  "limits": [
    "An HCCL AllToAll is downstream of preparation, sparse attention, RoPE and packing. Its launch and entry gaps are not measured slack or a saving.",
    "The original request can benefit from other DPs or earlier scheduling changes. Own-step TTFT sensitivity covers only directly attributed full batches. Host step entry before first token grants the entire step optimistic credit.",
    "Group/op identity matches only within each DP. No cross-DP worker-step match or physical clock synchronization is assumed. The separate candidate service has no per-timed-replay registration counters or peer timing; client text agreement covers these eight responses."
  ],
